course: dictionary
lesson: 5559
title: Making things longer
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Lengthen is a verb. It means to make something longer, or to become longer. Its opposite is shorten.
explain: You can lengthen a thing on purpose: «lengthen a skirt» means make the skirt longer. Things can also lengthen by themselves: «The days lengthen in spring» means the days get longer, with more daylight each day.
explain: In writing, you can lengthen a sentence by adding more words, adjectives or clauses. In maths, lengthen means to increase a length. Ask yourself: is the thing getting more length?
explain: Look at this context: «Your body is a building site that never closes: bones lengthen, teeth are swapped, hair and nails creep out.» The bones are growing longer while the body builds itself, so lengthen means become longer.
fact: Lengthen means to make something longer, or to become longer.
fact: «Lengthen a stride» means to take longer steps.
fact: «The days lengthen in spring» means there is more daylight each day in spring.
fact: Shorten is the opposite of lengthen.
fact: Lengthen, lengthens, lengthened and lengthening are all forms of the same verb.
exercise: «The days lengthen in spring.» What does lengthen mean here? | *Become longer | Become colder | Become shorter | Become dark
exercise: Mum says she will lengthen the skirt. What will she do? | Make it shorter | *Make it longer | Wash it | Throw it away
exercise: «Your body is a building site that never closes: bones lengthen, teeth are swapped, hair and nails creep out.» Which thing in this sentence lengthens? | Nails | Teeth | *Bones | Building site
test: What does it mean to lengthen a sentence? | *To make it longer | To cross it out | To make it shorter | To read it aloud
test: What happens when the days lengthen in spring? | The days get colder | The days get shorter | The days stop | *The days get longer
exam: Ella says lengthen means to shorten. Is she right? | *Yes, it means to cut short | Yes, it means to fold up | No, lengthen means to make longer or become longer | No, it means to paint
